'''Potion''' (Japanese: '''きずぐすり''' ''Salve'') is an {{TCGP|Item}} card in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. It is part of the {{TCGP|Promo-A}} series of cards.

==Card text==
{{TCGTrainerText
|class=Item
|rule=SWSH Item
|effect=Heal 20 damage from 1 of your Pokémon.
}}

==Release information==
Potion cards were first made available to purchase from the in-game {{TCGP|shop}} on October 30, 2024 worldwide (September 26, 2024 in New Zealand) for 2 Shop Tickets each. One copy of Potion is also awarded to players who complete the {{TCGP|Mission|mission}} "07: Attach Energy to your Benched Pokémon!" in the {{DL|Mission (TCG Pocket)|Battle Guide}}.

==Trivia==
* {{TCGP|Pokémon Center Lady}} has a more potent version of this card's effect, but as a {{TCGP|Supporter card}} instead of an Item card.
* This card's effect is identical to that of the {{TCG|Potion}} card in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] up to the Diamond & Pearl Series, when it allowed players to remove up to two damage counters (20 damage) from a Pokémon. The TCG card was altered in the {{TCG|Black & White}} expansion onward, after which it heals 30 damage instead.

===Origin===
* This card's illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Kalos Starter Set|Potion|37}} from the {{TCG|Kalos Starter Set}}.
* [[Potion]] is an item in the [[Pokémon games]] that heals damage. This card depicts the Potion as it appears in the majority of [[core series]] games, where its most common effect is also to heal up to 20 [[HP]].

